From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:32:13 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0302): bounded auto-reconnect, Cancel, and one session
 per connect

Reconnect (DEF-7, AC-24, AC-46):
- The policy lives in Rust (src/remotesmith_trust/reconnect.rs) and is
  applied in Session::msgbox. After a session was up, transient failures
  are retried even where upstream gives up ("Failed to connect...",
  "offline" while the host reboots); auth failures, refusals and identity
  problems never are. Delays 1, 2, 4, 8, 8... s, and the streak ends 60 s
  after its first failure. Upstream retried a narrower set forever.
- Cancel (retry dialog or the Connecting overlay) stops retrying, aborts
  the attempt in flight and shows "Disconnected - Reconnect" with the
  window kept open; only Reconnect there starts a new streak.
- A session the user closed is never reopened: Session::close marks it,
  and reconnect() and a late connect both honour the mark.
- The saved password is re-sent on reconnect as upstream does, so no
  re-entry is needed (AC-24).

Cancel and late results (AC-58): io_loop raced nothing against the UI
before; Client::start was awaited and a Close seen only afterwards, so a
late connect could still log in. The connect is now raced against Close
(dropping the future drops every LAN/ID attempt), and a connect that
completes after a lost Close is dropped. Input queued while connecting
is discarded; the host ignores anything sent before login, so nothing is
replayed.

Coalescing (AC-58): rapid Connect clicks while the first window is still
being created share that request instead of opening more windows; Rust
already keeps one connection per peer and type.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
